From 229dd16fb856d7e77a1fe8690e059a7ead7da6a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pavanteja295 <pavanteja295@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 10:14:08 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] Meshes that only the rig drives take no network offset

head_assets_eyes.npz appends MetaHuman's two eyeballs after the head. They are
rigid balls that rotate for gaze and nothing else, and an iris pattern does not
change, so there is no per-frame deviation from the rig for a network to predict.

Leaving them in the network's reach would not be neutral. The eyeball carries its
own texture coordinates and 35.8% of its texels land on head surface in the
shared atlas, so it would read the head's offset map and inherit the head's
per-frame nudge as noise on geometry that should be still.

The asset's own part table says where the head stops, so there is no threshold
and nothing to tune: triangles past the head's last one are rig-only, and their
blobs are forced back to the identity offset after the network runs. Identity is
not all zeros -- the 14 channels are an xyz shift, a scale MULTIPLIER, a rotation
quaternion in [r,x,y,z] order, a colour shift and an opacity shift, so scale is 1
and the quaternion is [1,0,0,0].

An asset without a part table behaves exactly as before, so runs on the old
head_assets.npz are unaffected and remain comparable.

  51,076 blobs, of which 3,072 are eyeball and rig-driven only

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
