From 64833a9474533f1f2a88ab433f293a8f0fdcc27b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pavanteja295 <pavanteja295@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 12:22:25 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] The MetaHuman changes that predate this branch having
 history

Everything here was already running the audio-render pipeline and had never
been committed. Recording it as one baseline so later work has a diff, not so
the individual changes get attribution they no longer have.

What is in it, from the findings that motivated each:

  scene/mesh_gaussian_model.py   Gaussians bound to a MetaHuman head instead of
                                 FLAME. Lazy per-frame mesh reads, because
                                 48,004 cooked meshes held in memory is 27.7 GB.
  gaussian_renderer/__init__.py  the 14 offset channels, and the canonical-mode
                                 rigid step.
  networks/dual_branch.py        condition width read off the model rather than
                                 hard-wired to 257, which is what let the FLAME
                                 path run at all.
  scene/gaussian_model.py        per-blob per-recording appearance. The colour
                                 and opacity channels the per-frame network was
                                 using as a recording lookup, given as an
                                 explicit parameter instead. +1.5 dB held out.
  train.py                       --per_take_appearance, --seed, and two loader
                                 workers rather than eight persistent ones,
                                 which was OOM-killing the host.
  utils/general_utils.py         safe_state takes the seed. It was hard-coded to
                                 58, so the two noise-floor arms of every sweep
                                 were byte-identical commands.
  scene/cluster_loader.py,
  scene/dataset_readers.py       identity arrays interned by content: static_offset
                                 and shape are per-recording, and were stored
                                 40,498 times. 2.33 GB.

Also ignores .venv, the hand-rolled .pre*/.bak shadow copies, and the upstream
FLAME assets, which are large and separately licensed.
