+| Component | Upstream | Here | Reason |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| CUDA toolkit | 11.7 | **12.8** | First toolkit that can target `sm_120`. Hard requirement. |
+| PyTorch | 2.0.1+cu117 | **2.8.0+cu128** | Needs `sm_120` in `torch.cuda.get_arch_list()`. 2.8.0 chosen over newer releases because it is the latest torch with a prebuilt `torch-scatter` wheel, which removes a source build. |
+| Python | 3.10 | 3.10 | Unchanged, and now load-bearing: stock `chumpy==0.70` calls `inspect.getargspec`, removed in Python 3.11. |
+| numpy | 1.22.3 | **1.23.5** | `>= 1.24` removes the `np.bool` / `np.float` aliases `chumpy` imports; `1.22.3` is below the floor of the scipy builds that support this stack. |
+| host compiler | distro gcc | **conda gcc 14** | nvcc 12.8 rejects gcc >= 15, which recent distros ship. Pulled in automatically by `cuda-nvcc`. |
+| `chumpy` | listed | kept | Not imported by any source file, but `pickle` needs it to load `flame2023.pkl`. |
 
