+
+    center_posed  == center_cano @ R + t
+    scaling_posed == scaling_cano           a rotation carries no scale
+    orien_posed   == R.T @ orien_cano       row-vector v @ R is column-form R.T v
+
+Checking those three covers all 48,004 Gaussians at once, and get_xyz is then checked
+end to end with a non-zero random _xyz shared by both models -- with _xyz at zero the
+orien term drops out and the test would pass while proving nothing about rotation.
+
+On the orien tolerance: ~0.08% of MetaHuman's faces are degenerate slivers (edges down
+to 15 um, area ~1e-9 m^2 against a 1.1e-06 median), and orthonormalising those in
+float32 is ill-conditioned, so rotate-then-orthonormalise differs from the reverse by up
+to 1.3e-02 on a handful of faces. That is a property of the mesh, present identically in
+posed mode, and it washes out of get_xyz because it is scaled by _xyz and the triangle's
