From bec8c26e377a83af830b8252e65fb3d2a63ab883 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pavanteja295 <pavanteja295@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 12:25:26 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] Run each detail branch only where its mask is

The four local branches convolve the whole 256x256 UV map and multiply by their
mask afterwards, so a branch covering 2.8% of the atlas costs exactly as much as
one covering 35.8%. Running each inside its mask's bounding box instead saves
2.46 ms of a 14.95 ms frame.

WHY IT IS EXACT

The block writes nothing outside the mask, because of the final multiply. An
output texel depends on inputs within the block's receptive field. So a box
holding every nonzero mask texel plus that margin gives every surviving output
its whole neighbourhood, and the arithmetic is identical. Outside the box both
versions are zero, since the box contains the mask by construction.

EXACT AT INFERENCE. A FEW ULPS APART IN TRAINING.

Forward is bit-identical, verified end to end on E1_pertake's trained weights:
32 frames x 69,776 blobs x 14 channels, 31,259,648 values, max absolute
difference 0.000e+00. The gradient with respect to the input is also exactly
identical.

PARAMETER gradients are not. They differ by 1.5e-08 to 1.1e-06 relative, against
a float32 epsilon of 1.19e-07: two to nine ULPs. A parameter gradient sums over
spatial positions, and the cropped version sums fewer of them -- the omitted
terms are all exactly zero, so the mathematics is the same and only the
accumulation order changes.

The consequence is small but real, and worth stating because this project scores
one-variable comparisons: a run TRAINED with cropping will drift away from one
trained without, the way a different cuDNN algorithm would. The model is not
worse, it is a different draw. Treat a cropped training run as a new seed, which
the measured noise floor already bounds at 0.16 dB and 0.0005 LPIPS. Inference
on an existing checkpoint has no such caveat and can be switched on freely.

TWO THINGS THAT WOULD MAKE IT WRONG, BOTH GUARDED

The margin is DERIVED from the block, never typed. It is 2 today because the
block is two 3x3 convolutions and a 1x1. Add a conv or a dilation and a
hard-coded 2 goes silently wrong, because the output is still masked: you would
get a plausible face with a thin band of the wrong values around every region.
Measured, margin 1 is off by 3.9e-02 and margin 0 by 1.1e-01, and the test
asserts that both still differ -- if they ever stop, the argument is wrong.

The box comes from ANY NONZERO WEIGHT, never a threshold. Our own masks are
binary so the two agree and this cannot be caught on them. MetaHuman's painted
masks are feathered down to 0.004, and a > 0.5 box is 3.6x smaller on the lips
while discarding 38% of that mask's real support -- with no symptom, because the
render still looks like a face and only loses every region's soft edge. The test
covers it with a synthetic feathered mask.

The boxes are computed at construction from the mask tensors and stored nowhere
else. A cached box goes stale the moment a mask is rebuilt, which is what
happened to eye_region on 2026-09-17, in place, mid-experiment.

box=None keeps every existing caller unchanged.

Per branch, cropped against full: nose 4.81x, forehead 2.60x, eye 2.46x, lips
1.08x. Lips barely moves because its box is 89.5% of the atlas, which is itself
a signal that that mask is wrong rather than a limit of this change.

NOT DONE HERE

forward_once() already exists, is called by nothing, and is another 2.92 ms: the
encoder runs every frame on a reference image set once at construction. It is
inference-only -- during training the encoder's own weights move, so its output
is not constant.
