+"""Cropping a detail branch to its mask's box must be BIT-identical, not close.
+
+Unlike almost everything else in this pipeline, the right answer here is computable:
+the full-map result is the reference. So these are equality assertions, not tolerance
+ones, and a wrong box, a wrong mask and an off-by-one in the scatter all fail the same
+line.
+
+Five things are checked, and the two negative ones matter as much as the positive:
+
+  1. the margin is DERIVED from the block, and is 2 for two 3x3 convs and a 1x1
+  2. cropped == full, exactly, on all four real masks
+  3. margin 0 and margin 1 DIFFER. If they ever stop differing the reasoning is
+     wrong, because the claim rests on the receptive field being load-bearing
+  4. a feathered mask's box follows its whole support, not its > 0.5 part. Our own
+     masks are binary so this cannot be caught on them; MetaHuman's painted masks
+     go down to 0.004 and a > 0.5 box silently drops 38% of the lips mask
+  5. an empty mask raises rather than producing a silent zero branch
+
