From c07a9cc21426caa535ac493ae90e5cea198ad45c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pavanteja295 <pavanteja295@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 18:34:50 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] Rig-only meshes keep the per-recording appearance: the
 other way is worse

Tested, because the argument against it was good. The per-recording offset exists
to absorb what CHANGES between takes, and measured on G2 its spread across
recordings orders exactly that way:

  collar 0.2446   hair 0.0974   face 0.0522   eyeball 0.0281

Enamel and an iris cannot change between takes, so an offset there looked like
free capacity whose only use was to overfit which recording a frame came from.
Denying it to them cost more than any other change tried in four runs:

  appearance ON  rig-only meshes   PSNR 21.8752  LPIPS 0.1085   (G2)
  appearance OFF                   PSNR 21.8183  LPIPS 0.1065   (G5)

Smallest is not the same as unnecessary. The three recordings differ in lighting,
and an eye is lit by the room as much as skin is.

